Patch 7921 (experimental, rollback netcode): the lwmutex census walks the occupied slots only and caches readability per page.

runtime/ppu/ppu_sysprx.cpp: the lwmutex table records the slots it claims (slots are never freed), and ps3_lwmutex_census walks that
list instead of all 65,536 slots. The census's readability check is cached per 4 KB guest page (commit and protection work in whole
pages) in 4,096 direct-mapped slots, keyed by the census epoch and the layout generation of patch 7920; an address that straddles a
page checks both pages. Measured with the rollback snapshot: VirtualQuery on the write-watched reservation costs ~0.19 ms a call, and
the 128-slot cache that did not cache straddling addresses left ~12 calls (2.3 ms) in every frozen census. Counters for the snapshot's
census profile (JSP_SNAPSHOT_CENSUS_PROF=1): g_lwm_rd_hits, g_lwm_rd_vq, g_lwm_rd_vq_ns, g_lwm_rd_uncacheable, g_lwm_rd_invalidates.
Applies after 7920.

